Z||000000||danny boy||03-21-2001||11:02 PM|||| Top story in the Metro-Region section of the Dominion post Mar 21,2K1 (Morgantown, WV local paper)<P>KINGWOOD -  A small red car, sitting in the midle of a rough Preston County backroad, was surrounded by dogs firefighters and police Tuesday, as they looked for a missing Masontown man.<BR>  Scott Lee Cummings,46,of Masontown, was last seen about 2AM Saturday at the Masontown Marathon.Cummings' brother and and a family friend found his Red '85 Pontiac Fiero about 12:30 PM Tuesday,several miles up a dirt road that circles from the Long Hollow Road near Chippewa Lake, outside Kingwood.<BR>  The road passes through recently timbered forests papered with no hunting or tres passing signs put up by hunting clubs. A jacket identified as Cummings' lat hung up in briars up the road from the car.<BR>...Cummings was dispondent when his family last spoke with him....<P> A few months ago, Scott bought my 86 base coupe for his friend and some parts for his car. I kept in touch with him up until this weekend when he disappeared. Friday night I called his house to see if Brian(his friend with my old car) would come down so we could fix his steering column and give me my rear swaybar back. He said as soon as Scott got home from work he'd call me and let me know. He never came home.<BR>Scotts wife was worried when I talked to her sunday night, but didn't think anything was wrong."If you see Scott, tell him he's missing", she said and laughed as we hung up.<BR> They found him today. No word yet on the acual cause of Death, but Brian said he was worried Scott was going to take some pills to try to kill himself.He did.<BR> ||||reg||1
