Z||000008||AkursedX||03-23-2001||12:19 AM||||Sorry to hear about that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>In 9 months, I went through the suicides of my best friend and 2 other very close friends.  I almost followed that path myself...but I'm still here.  I just hate to see people kill themselves.  It is so hard on so many people.  I believe that suicide is the most selfish act you can possibly commit, and i have a very hard time feeling pity for anyone who commits such an act.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||03-24-2001||05:51 PM||||We ahd asomewhat similar thing happen here on Thursday.<P>I got up at 6am as usual to get ready to head downtown to register for my classes. The news was telling not to take I-675 North bound because it was closed. I think, no biggy, I'll take I-75 instead. Just as I am leaving school around 2pm, a friend calls, saying he is stuck on 675 Northbound, and that no-one is moving and he thinks it is shut down. He hadn't heard not to take that route. <P>Turns out a Cincinatti man stole a car, drove it up here, and parked in the median. He got out, and then stood at the side of the highway and waited for a semi to approach. Stepped right out in front of one. They weren't even able to ID the remains. <P>Just thinking about it makes me shiver. I drive that route everyday, and it happened only about 15 miles North of where I live. I'm just glad I wasn't around to see it happen.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||03-25-2001||12:12 PM||||How cowardly!!<BR>Think how that's gonna affect the guy who was driving the semi.<BR>Jeez, it's one thing to do it to himself, but to drag some innocent person into the situation? ||||reg||8
